abstract: >
  A calibrated simulator of mobile-game real-time-bidding auctions that retains
  the ground truth for every auction, won or lost, and a benchmark built on it in
  which the data stay fixed while the training method varies. Funnel outcomes and
  the top competing bid are generated on all rows, so methods can be scored on the
  auctions the bidder lost, which no real advertising log records. Four censoring
  operators reduce the master table to the views real platforms hold: a demand-side
  platform alone, plus measurement data, plus auction price data, and all three
  combined. Software is MIT licensed; data, including the deposited datasets, is
  CC BY 4.0.
keywords:
  - real-time bidding
  - computational advertising
  - synthetic data
  - causal inference
  - selection bias
  - censored data
  - counterfactual evaluation
  - benchmark
